Source: https://github.com/NVIDIA/BigVGAN
License: MIT
Files: crates/pmetal-vocoder/ (the test fixtures under tests/fixtures hold values
computed by the reference code and a copy of a release's config.json)

BigVGAN in turn adapts HiFi-GAN (Kong et al., MIT), the Snake activation
(Ziyin et al.; implementation by Edward Dixon, MIT), alias-free-torch
(junjun3518, Apache 2.0), julius (Defossez, MIT), the Descript audio codec's
multi-scale mel loss (MIT), Vocos' multi-band discriminator (MIT) and Amphion's
CQT discriminator (MIT). The constant-Q transform follows nnAudio (MIT) and
the sample-rate converter follows torchaudio's windowed-sinc kernel (BSD
2-Clause); the mel filterbank follows librosa (ISC).


